examples.question_text:
Complete a forward and backward scan of this network. Durations are in minutes; the dashed activity has duration $0$. State the minimum completion time, the EST of $G$ and the LST of $F$. Each box holds EST on the left and LST on the right.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0); \coordinate (U) at (2,1.5); \coordinate (V) at (2,-1.5); \coordinate (W) at (4.5,1.5); \coordinate (X) at (4.5,-1.5); \coordinate (Y) at (7,0); \coordinate (Z) at (9,0); \coordinate (T) at (11,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(U) node[midway,above left] {$A,6$};
\draw[->] (S)--(V) node[midway,below left] {$B,4$};
\draw[->] (U)--(W) node[midway,above] {$C,2$};
\draw[->] (V)--(X) node[midway,below] {$D,3$};
\draw[->,dashed] (W)--(X) node[midway,left] {$0$};
\draw[->] (W)--(Y) node[midway,above right] {$E,4$};
\draw[->] (X)--(Y) node[midway,below right] {$F,2$};
\draw[->] (Y)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$G,3$};
\draw[->] (Z)--(T) node[midway,above] {$H,2$};
\foreach \v/\dy in {S/0.7,U/0.7,V/-0.7,W/0.7,X/-0.7,Y/-0.7,Z/-0.7,T/-0.7}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt); \begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=\dy cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\end{scope}}
\node[left] at (S) {Start}; \node[right] at (T) {Finish};
\node[below=10pt,text=black] at (S) {$S$};
\node[above=30pt,text=black] at (U) {$U$};
\node[below=30pt,text=black] at (V) {$V$};
\node[above=30pt,text=black] at (W) {$W$};
\node[below=30pt,text=black] at (X) {$X$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (Z) {$Z$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Scan forward, adding durations and taking the larger total where paths meet. The dummy contributes $0$.
$\begin{aligned}E_S&=0\\E_U&=0+6=6\\E_V&=0+4=4\\E_W&=6+2=8\\E_X&=\max(4+3,8+0)=8\\E_Y&=\max(8+4,8+2)=12\\E_Z&=12+3=15\\E_T&=15+2=17\end{aligned}$
Copy $17$ into the finish LST box. Scan backward, subtracting durations and taking the smaller result where paths split.
$\begin{aligned}L_T&=17\\L_Z&=17-2=15\\L_Y&=15-3=12\\L_X&=12-2=10\\L_W&=\min(12-4,10-0)=8\\L_V&=10-3=7\\L_U&=8-2=6\\L_S&=\min(6-6,7-4)=0\end{aligned}$
Both start values are $0$. The completed boxes are shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{scanblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (S) at (0,0); \coordinate (U) at (2,1.5); \coordinate (V) at (2,-1.5); \coordinate (W) at (4.5,1.5); \coordinate (X) at (4.5,-1.5); \coordinate (Y) at (7,0); \coordinate (Z) at (9,0); \coordinate (T) at (11,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(U) node[midway,above left] {$A,6$};
\draw[->] (S)--(V) node[midway,below left] {$B,4$};
\draw[->] (U)--(W) node[midway,above] {$C,2$};
\draw[->] (V)--(X) node[midway,below] {$D,3$};
\draw[->] (W)--(Y) node[midway,above right] {$E,4$};
\draw[->] (X)--(Y) node[midway,below right] {$F,2$};
\draw[->,dashed] (W)--(X) node[midway,left] {$0$};
\draw[->] (Y)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$G,3$};
\draw[->] (Z)--(T) node[midway,above] {$H,2$};
\foreach \v/\dy/\e/\l in {S/0.7/0/0,U/0.7/6/6,V/-0.7/4/7,W/0.7/8/8,X/-0.7/8/10,Y/-0.7/12/12,Z/-0.7/15/15,T/-0.7/17/17}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt);\begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=\dy cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\node[text=scanblue] at (-0.25,0) {$\e$};\node[text=scanblue] at (0.25,0) {$\l$};\end{scope}}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (T) {Finish};
\node[below=10pt,text=black] at (S) {$S$};
\node[above=30pt,text=black] at (U) {$U$};
\node[below=30pt,text=black] at (V) {$V$};
\node[above=30pt,text=black] at (W) {$W$};
\node[below=30pt,text=black] at (X) {$X$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (Y) {$Y$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (Z) {$Z$};
\node[above=10pt,text=black] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The minimum completion time is $17$ minutes. Activity $G$ begins at $Y$, so its EST is $12$ minutes. Only $F$ leaves $X$, so its LST is $12-2=10$ minutes.

examples.question_text:
This is part of a larger network. Each box holds EST on the left and LST on the right; times are in hours. Activity $P$ is the only activity leaving $U$ and the only activity arriving at $V$. Find $p$ and $q$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (U) at (0,0);\coordinate (V) at (4,0);
\draw[->] (U)--(V) node[midway,below] {$P,7$};
\foreach \v/\e/\l in {U/5/q,V/p/14}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt);\begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=0.7cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\node at (-0.25,0) {$\e$};\node at (0.25,0) {$\l$};\end{scope}\node[below] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Find $p$ by scanning forward from the EST at $U$.
$\begin{aligned}p&=5+7\\&=12\end{aligned}$
Find $q$ by scanning backward from the LST at $V$.
$\begin{aligned}q&=14-7\\&=7\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{scanblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (U) at (0,0);\coordinate (V) at (4,0);
\draw[->] (U)--(V) node[midway,below] {$P,7$};
\foreach \v in {U,V}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt);\begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=0.7cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\end{scope}\node[below] at (\v) {$\v$};}
\node at (-0.25,0.7) {$5$};\node[text=scanblue] at (0.25,0.7) {$7$};\node[text=scanblue] at (3.75,0.7) {$12$};\node at (4.25,0.7) {$14$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The forward and backward scans are complete. Each box holds EST on the left and LST on the right; all times are in days. Find the unknown duration $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (U) at (2,1.5);\coordinate (V) at (2,-1.5);\coordinate (W) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (T) at (7,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(U) node[midway,above left] {$A,4$};\draw[->] (S)--(V) node[midway,below left] {$B,8$};\draw[->] (U)--(W) node[midway,above right] {$C,x$};\draw[->] (V)--(W) node[midway,below right] {$D,3$};\draw[->] (W)--(T) node[midway,above] {$E,5$};
\foreach \v/\dy/\e/\l in {S/0.7/0/0,U/0.7/4/4,V/-0.7/8/11,W/-0.7/14/14,T/-0.7/19/19}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt);\begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=\dy cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\node at (-0.25,0) {$\e$};\node at (0.25,0) {$\l$};\end{scope}}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (T) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The EST at the merge is $14$. The arriving total through $D$ is $8+3=11$, so the total through $C$ must be $14$.
$\begin{aligned}4+x&=14\\x&=14-4\\x&=10\end{aligned}$
The duration of $C$ is $10$ days. Backward scanning confirms the given LST at its tail: $14-10=4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{scanblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (U) at (2,1.5);\coordinate (V) at (2,-1.5);\coordinate (W) at (4.5,0);\coordinate (T) at (7,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(U) node[midway,above left] {$A,4$};\draw[->] (S)--(V) node[midway,below left] {$B,8$};\draw[->] (U)--(W) node[midway,above right,text=scanblue] {$C,10$};\draw[->] (V)--(W) node[midway,below right] {$D,3$};\draw[->] (W)--(T) node[midway,above] {$E,5$};
\foreach \v/\dy/\e/\l in {S/0.7/0/0,U/0.7/4/4,V/-0.7/8/11,W/-0.7/14/14,T/-0.7/19/19}{\fill (\v) circle (1.5pt);\begin{scope}[shift={(\v)},yshift=\dy cm]\draw (-0.5,-0.25) rectangle (0.5,0.25);\draw (0,-0.25)--(0,0.25);\node at (-0.25,0) {$\e$};\node at (0.25,0) {$\l$};\end{scope}}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (T) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
